#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Rebuild data/out/conditions-sources.json for the Out app's Explore > Conditions lane.

What it does: writes the catalog of trail, park, beach, ice and road condition sources and the
dog-park rules. Every record is typed in below from pages read on 2026-10-29; the script makes
NO network calls and does not poll any feed.

What it records (fetched by hand that day): Fellowship of the Wheel (Trailforks region ids), Green
Mountain Club alerts (WordPress JSON), Burlington and South Burlington alert RSS, Burlington beach
tracker and Greenway / skating-rink ArcGIS layers, VTrans Compass XML closures, state park, Catamount,
Sleepy Hollow, Hinesburg Town Forest, Local Motion pages, and each dog park's own page.

What still needs a hand:
  - The current_status_snapshot text and `verified` dates are a 2026-10-29 snapshot; re-read the
    pages and edit the records here before rerunning.
  - A poller that reads the nine machine-readable feeds (feed_url / feed_type) is not written yet.
  - Fellowship of the Wheel trail status needs a Trailforks API key; Burlington's leash ordinance
    (ecode360) and the Williston town site block scripts.

Usage: python3 scripts/out/build_out_conditions.py [out_path]
"""
